menu "Car control"

config CAR_MOTOR_CONTROL
    bool "Enable encoder and serial motor control (standby at boot)"
    default y
    help
        Both motor channels remain in standby after initialization.
        Send enable, then a/b/ab percentage commands to start motors.
        Left encoder GPIO17/18, right encoder GPIO1/2. UART/USB accept
        motor commands. Disconnect retains output.

config CAR_BLE_UART
    bool "Enable BLE UART command input"
    default n
    depends on CAR_MOTOR_CONTROL && BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED
    help
        Optional Nordic UART Service command input and encoder notifications.
        Disabled while using an external wireless UART bridge.

config CAR_PID_TUNER
    bool "Enable LLM-PID-Tuner serial protocol (CSV telemetry + SET P/I/D)"
    default y
    depends on CAR_MOTOR_CONTROL
    help
        Streams timestamp_ms,setpoint,input,pwm,error,p,i,d at the period
        set by CAR_PID_TUNER_PERIOD_MS (default 20 Hz) and
        accepts the uppercase commands used by KINGSTON-115/llm-pid-tuner:
        STATUS, SET P:.. I:.. D:.., SET KP:.. KI:.. KD:.., SETPOINT:.., RESET.
        SET applies the attitude-loop gains while the car keeps balancing and
        arms the loop automatically once the car is upright and still.
        While enabled, the human-readable attitude and encoder lines are
        suppressed so the host parser sees an uninterrupted CSV stream.
        Lowercase commands remain the normal manual interface.
        Also set CAR_ENCODER_ONLY_LOG to 0 in main/car_log_mode.h.

config CAR_PID_TUNER_AUTO_ARM
    bool "Allow the tuner link to arm the balance loop on SET"
    default y
    depends on CAR_PID_TUNER
    help
        Without an explicit balance arm, the host tool cannot start the loop.
        With this option, the first valid SET (Kp > 0) captures the current
        tilt as upright reference when no calibration exists and arms only if
        the car is within 10 degrees, slower than 5 deg/s and both wheels are
        below 10 counts/s. Disarm with standby or balance off.

config CAR_PID_TUNER_PERIOD_MS
    int "CSV report period (ms)"
    range 20 1000
    default 50
    depends on CAR_PID_TUNER
    help
        Period of the timestamp_ms,setpoint,input,pwm,error,p,i,d line.
        Default 50 ms (20 Hz). Wireless bridges (Bluetooth, wireless
        DAPLink, 433 MHz) may not forward the host SET within the host's
        1 s write timeout while 20 Hz telemetry is streaming; use 200
        (5 Hz) or 100 (10 Hz) for those links. A slower stream makes each
        tuning round longer, so reduce the host BUFFER_SIZE accordingly
        (for example 50 at 5 Hz gives about 10 s per round).

config CAR_TB6612_SCOPE_TEST
    bool "Enable TB6612FNG serial command control for scope tests (no motors)"
    default n
    depends on !CAR_MOTOR_CONTROL
    help
        Starts in standby and accepts serial commands to control both motor
        channels, independently of the IMU. Waveforms hold until the next command.
        Intended for oscilloscope tests WITHOUT motors attached.
        Disable before implementing another motor controller.

endmenu
